See how every log line now has `"mycompany-trace-id":"tracker-7e073c4f-2144-47ce-172881be0954"`

If the custom image has one interface, it can be accessed by set route '/v1/models/{servername}:predict'. But if the custom image has >=2 interfaces, how to access others?
This is a custom flask server example, i can call `hello_world` by `curl http://xxx//v1/models/my-custom-sample:predict`, but i cannot call `hello_world_test`.
```python
import os

from flask import Flask

app = Flask(__name__)

@app.route('/v1/models/my-custom-sample:test')
def hello_world_test():
    target = os.environ.get('TARGET', 'World')
    return 'test Hello {}!\n'.format(target)

@app.route('/v1/models/my-custom-sample:predict')
def hello_world():
    target = os.environ.get('TARGET', 'World')
    return 'Hello {}!\n'.format(target)

if __name__ == "__main__":
    app.run(debug=True,host='0.0.0.0',port=int(os.environ.get('PORT', 8080)))

```

I want to access the 2 inferfaces both.
